# Build output
build/
tmp/
releases/

# ESP-IDF
# sdkconfig is generated, but it is also the only record of which board the
# firmware was configured for. Losing it once silently swapped the build from
# esp32_S3_DevKitC_1_voice/16MB back to esp32_S3_DevKitC_1/8MB, and nothing in
# git could show that it had happened. Track the one the project actually
# builds; keep any generated later (test_apps and friends) out.
sdkconfig
!/application/edge_agent/sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
sdkconfig.priv
sdkconfig.bmgr_board.old
# The component manager resolves this once and then carries it forward. A
# re-solve is not reproducible: two dependency rules in lua_module_vision key
# off Kconfig symbols that do not exist on a board without a camera, so solving
# from scratch never converges and the project stops building. Losing this file
# cost a working build, and nothing in git could put it back.
dependencies.lock
!/application/edge_agent/dependencies.lock
managed_components/

